{"id":"579476637","kind":"article","title":"记忆的双组分模型","author":"Piotr Wozniak","original_authors":["Piotr Wozniak"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Two_component_model_of_memory"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2022-11-01","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":8,"comment_count":2,"minutes":3,"chars":1255,"keywords":["双组分记忆模型","记忆稳定性","可提取性","间隔效应","SuperMemo"],"summary":"条目介绍长期记忆的双组分模型：稳定性 S 描述记忆在未提取、未受干扰时可维持多久，可提取性 R 描述当下成功提取的概率。作者称这一区分能避免把不同性质混称“记忆强度”，并用间隔效应解释稳定性如何增长，同时指出 SuperMemo 的 SM-17 实践支持该模型。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/579476637","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"模型概述"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"生物学功能"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"起源"},{"id":"sec-4","level":2,"title":"意义"}],"html":"<h2 id=\"sec-1\">模型概述</h2><p data-pid=\"wi64_BD6\">长期记忆的双组分模型断言，两个相互独立的变量足以描述人类大脑中<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Atomic_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">原子记忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>的状态。</p><ul><li data-pid=\"xjM3Zc4E\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>（S）决定了在未被干扰和未被提取的情况下，记忆可以保持多长时间<br/> </li><li data-pid=\"5Z98n31P\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>（R）决定了在给定时刻，记忆可以被提取的概率<br/> </li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">生物学功能</h2><p data-pid=\"8dThVKDk\">我们相信，该模型体现出为了阻止新皮质网络中灾难性<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Interference\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">干扰</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>的进化。记忆<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>将降低突触权重的变动，并阻止很有用的记忆被<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Forgetting\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">遗忘</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>。另一方面，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spacing_effect\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>保护记忆免于在频繁接触中达到过高的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>（参见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Structural_and_molecular_mechanisms_of_the_spacing_effect\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应的结构与分子机理</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup>）。</p><p data-pid=\"rHHzlteW\"><b>记忆的双组分模型消除了可塑性-稳定性的两难问题</b></p><h2 id=\"sec-3\">起源</h2><p data-pid=\"mEqLtlUj\">在记忆研究文献中，「记忆强度」这一定义不明确的术语通常代表稳定性（S）或可提取性（R）。这导致了大量混淆，并延缓了记忆研究的进展。在 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Optimization_of_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">1990</a> 和 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/ANE1995\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">1995</a> 这两篇论文中，我们已经从理论上证明了这两个变量——<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">S</a> 和 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">R</a>——足以描述记忆的状态。</p><p data-pid=\"_9GUXtLy\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Robert_Bjork\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Bjork</a> 的独立研究 <i>New Theory of Disuse</i>（1992）使用了类似的术语「储存强度」和「提取强度」。另见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Jost‘s_Law\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">约斯特定律</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"sb4OwWvv\">要了解模型的发展历史，请参阅：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Two_components_of_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆的两个组成成分</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup></p><h2 id=\"sec-4\">意义</h2><p data-pid=\"LCT_5MTo\">该模型可用于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Modelling_molecular_and_structural_long-term_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">长期记忆的分子与结构性质分析</a>。</p><p data-pid=\"1cp1ujJ6\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a> 的 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Algorithm_SM-17\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SM-17 算法</a>的实现和实践结果证明了双组分模型的正确性。该模型和算法使人们可以定量研究记忆。例如：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/How_much_knowledge_can_human_brain_hold\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">人脑能容纳多少知识</a>？</p><p data-pid=\"5rOzqtwz\">该模型提供了支持<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Grandmother_cell\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">祖母细胞</a>理论的证据。参见： <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/The_truth_about_grandmother_cells\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">祖母细胞的真相</a></p><blockquote data-pid=\"hBmQaziT\">本<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Glossary\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">术语表</a>条目用于解释《<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Problem_of_Schooling\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复的历史</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-10\"><a href=\"#ref-10\">[10]</a></sup>》（2017）作者：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Piotr_Wozniak\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">彼得·沃兹尼亚克</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-11\"><a href=\"#ref-11\">[11]</a></sup></blockquote><figure data-size=\"normal\"><img class=\"origin_image zh-lightbox-thumb\" data-original-token=\"v2-2a62b38d8572f8877242e2d9e49d63df\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://picx.zhimg.com/v2-2a62b38d8572f8877242e2d9e49d63df_r.jpg\" width=\"500\"/><figcaption>SuperMemo: Changes in two variables of long-term memory: retrievability and stability</figcaption></figure><blockquote data-pid=\"N3ZJwzbE\"> 图：示例<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Piece_of_knowledge\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">知识片段</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-12\"><a href=\"#ref-12\">[12]</a></sup>的记忆状态随时间的变化。横轴表示跨越整个<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Repetition_history\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">重复历史</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-13\"><a href=\"#ref-13\">[13]</a></sup>的时间。顶部面板展示了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-14\"><a href=\"#ref-14\">[14]</a></sup>（为了便于分析，进行十次方变换，R^10）。灰色的可提取性网格标记了 R=99%, R=98% 等标签。中部面板用深蓝色展示了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Optimum_interval\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最优间隔</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-15\"><a href=\"#ref-15\">[15]</a></sup>。复习日期由蓝色垂线和浅蓝色标签标记。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Optimum_interval\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最优间隔</a>的末端对应的 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">R</a> 为 90% 左右，由红色垂线标记（仅当实际复习<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Interval\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔</a>大等于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Optimum_interval\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最优间隔</a>时）。底部面板可视化了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>（为了便于分析，以 <code>ln(S)/ln(days)</code> 的形式展示）。该图表指出 ，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>在最初几次<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>很低时的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Repetition\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">复习</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-16\"><a href=\"#ref-16\">[16]</a></sup>中下降得很快（指数型）。然而在第 7 次复习后，经过十年时间，可提取性从 100% 只下降到了 94%。所有的数值都来自实际的复习历史和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Three_component_model_of_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆的三变量模型</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-17\"><a href=\"#ref-17\">[17]</a></sup>。</blockquote><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"a_fl67cK\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 <a class=\"member_mention\" data-hash=\"4c592f496dc33822b560b382907ff1d0\" data-hovercard=\"p$b$4c592f496dc33822b560b382907ff1d0\" href=\"https://www.zhihu.com/people/L.M.Sherlock\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">@叶峻峣</a> <br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Two_component_model_of_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Two component model of memory - supermemo.guru</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 原子记忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"608600880\" href=\"#/post/608600880\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 记忆稳定性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559298549\" href=\"#/post/559298549\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 记忆可提取性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559819340\" href=\"#/post/559819340\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 干扰 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"269974053\" href=\"#/post/269974053\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 遗忘 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"558542113\" href=\"#/post/558542113\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 间隔效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"424603970\" href=\"#/post/424603970\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 间隔效应的结构与分子机理 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"288609114\" href=\"#/post/288609114\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 约斯特定律 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"401155017\" href=\"#/post/401155017\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 05 1988：记忆的两个组成成分 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"99505568\" href=\"#/post/99505568\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-10\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-10\">↩</a> 0 目录《间隔重复的历史》 <a href=\"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/375379522\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/375379522</a></li><li id=\"ref-11\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-11\">↩</a> 彼得·沃兹尼亚克 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"303204832\" href=\"#/post/303204832\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-12\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-12\">↩</a> 条目 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"571700330\" href=\"#/post/571700330\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-13\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-13\">↩</a> 重复历史 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"574628398\" href=\"#/post/574628398\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-14\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-14\">↩</a> 记忆可提取性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559819340\" href=\"#/post/559819340\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-15\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-15\">↩</a> 最优间隔 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"584041631\" href=\"#/post/584041631\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-16\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-16\">↩</a> 重复 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"572444486\" href=\"#/post/572444486\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-17\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-17\">↩</a> 记忆的三组分模型 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"580945538\" href=\"#/post/580945538\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"574139400","title":"解释学","author":"Issa Rice","votes":16,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"579583132","title":"如何提升我的创造力？","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":76,"minutes":6,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"99505568","title":"05 1988：记忆的两个组成成分","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":49,"minutes":20,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"401155017","title":"JOST'S LAW 约斯特定律","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":9,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"608600880","title":"原子记忆","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":11,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"279166945","title":"间隔效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":21,"minutes":3,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔效应」· Andy Matuschak"},{"id":"2020082520478201804","title":"记忆模型的数学形式化","author":"Giacomo Randazzo","votes":17,"minutes":14,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「可提取性」· Giacomo Randazzo"},{"id":"1907760881749718522","title":"间隔重复记忆系统：已取得长足进步","author":"Domenic Denicola","votes":261,"minutes":12,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「记忆稳定性」· Domenic Denicola"},{"id":"649655080","title":"解释 FSRS（上篇）：算法描述与运作原理","author":"ClarityInMadness","votes":110,"minutes":6,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「记忆稳定性」· ClarityInMadness"},{"id":"1941069300833190267","title":"感知内容的间隔重复","author":"Giacomo Randazzo","votes":62,"minutes":21,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「可提取性」· Giacomo Randazzo"}],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2024783376297596199","title":"如何看待“学生和家长仅仅希望高中不要凌晨五点半就到校，多睡一个小时，就被指责为想搞快乐教育”这句话？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":804,"minutes":82,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 804 赞同","evidence":"逐对核验：回答用该译文的直接脚注锚点指向文章标题或对应的特定术语。"},{"id":"3333217724","title":"学习是一件反人类的事情吗？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":546,"minutes":90,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 546 赞同","evidence":"正文中有明确指向该译文的知乎内链/链接卡，按直接提及记为1级。"},{"id":"3265798117","title":"学习到底是快乐的，还是痛苦的?","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":422,"minutes":88,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 422 赞同","evidence":"正文明确链接到目标词条标题。"},{"id":"1991462005836637138","title":"各位能分享一下自己做本科生科研的经历吗？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":326,"minutes":5,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 326 赞同","evidence":"正文明确使用该译文的唯一术语标题“记忆的双组分模型”，并解释其稳定性与可提取性，足以指向目标；记为1级。"},{"id":"3071397693","title":"真正的教育应该是快乐的，不是吗？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":196,"minutes":88,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 196 赞同","evidence":"正文通过准确的译文标题或原生引文锚直接指向目标；仅按标题/关键词提及计 1 级。"}]}